PRACTICAL – 3
Title:

Static Analysis of Mobile Application using MobSF

Aim:

To perform static analysis of an Android application using Mobile Security Framework (MobSF) deployed with Docker.

Objectives:
To understand static analysis of Android applications
To install and configure MobSF using Docker
To analyze APK files without executing them
To identify permissions, vulnerabilities, and insecure configurations
To study application source code and manifest details
Procedure:
(i) Install Docker

Open terminal and run:

sudo apt update
sudo apt install docker.io docker-compose -y

Start Docker service:

sudo systemctl start docker
sudo systemctl enable docker

Verify installation:

docker --version
(ii) Download MobSF

Clone MobSF repository:

git clone --depth 1 https://github.com/MobSF/Mobile-Security-Framework-MobSF.git

Navigate into directory:

cd Mobile-Security-Framework-MobSF
(iii) Run MobSF using Docker

Start MobSF container:

sudo docker-compose up
(iv) Open MobSF Dashboard

Open browser and visit:

http://127.0.0.1:8000
(v) Upload APK File
Click Upload & Analyze
Select APK file (diva.apk)
Wait for analysis completion
(vi) Analyze Security Report

Observe:

Application permissions
Manifest configuration
Hardcoded secrets and API keys
Activities and services
Vulnerability reports and security score
(vii) Review Decompiled Code
Open source code section
Analyze Java code and AndroidManifest.xml
Observation:
MobSF was successfully deployed using Docker
APK file was uploaded and analyzed successfully
Application permissions and components were identified
Security vulnerabilities and insecure configurations were detected
Decompiled source code and manifest details were displayed
Result:

Static analysis of the Android application was successfully performed using MobSF deployed through Docker. The framework identified permissions, application components, and potential security vulnerabilities without executing the application.

Viva Questions:
Q: What is MobSF?

👉 Mobile Security Framework used for mobile application security analysis.

Q: What is static analysis?

👉 Analysis of application code without running the application.

Q: Why use Docker for MobSF?

👉 Docker provides isolated and consistent deployment environment.

Q: What information does MobSF provide?

👉 Permissions, vulnerabilities, manifest details, source code, APIs, and security risks.

